Sam is a psychologist who back in the 1980s was working with homeless people in New York City. And the ideas that came out of the work he was doing are pretty foundational to how people think about solving homelessness today. Back then, Sam's typical day was spent driving around the streets of New York in a van with a nurse and a psychiatrist essentially making sidewalk house calls to the city's homeless.
山姆是一位心理学家，在 20 世纪 80 年代，他在纽约市从事无家可归者的工作。他当时的工作所产生的理念，对于今天人们如何看待解决无家可归问题起到了非常基础的作用。在那时，山姆典型的一天是和一名护士以及一名精神科医生一起，开着一辆面包车在纽约的街道上四处转悠，本质上是为全市的无家可归者提供路边上门服务。

5
00:01:31.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Two or three of us would be in the van with a driver, and we would receive referrals, all kinds of people would call and say, I have to, I want to refer somebody to you. I saw them on the corner of 65th and Park. They're ranting and they don't look well at all. And they're standing out in the middle of the traffic, trying to convert the drivers into some belief system. The 1980s was really the beginning of homelessness as we now know it, mainly because of rising income inequality
我们车上有两三个人加上司机，我们会接到转介，各种各样的人会打电话说，我必须、我想向你们转介一个人。我在65街和公园大道的转角看到了他们。他们在长篇大论，看起来状态非常糟糕。他们站在车流中间，试图把司机们转化到某种信仰体系中。20世纪80年代确实是我们现在所知的无家可归现象的开端，主要是由于收入不平等加剧，

6
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:46.000
and the dismantling of a lot of social programs like public housing. The crack up a Demick and deinstitutionalization certainly didn't help matters either. Anyway, homelessness was particularly exploding in New York, and there was a feeling that some of the people on the streets might be a danger to themselves or to others. And if they met that criteria, we would bring them to the hospital voluntarily if we could accomplish that, persuade them to go or involuntarily if necessary, we would call the police and they would be taken sometimes in handcuffs to the Bellevue psychiatric emergency room. Sam thought there were times when, in voluntary commitment,
以及公共住房等许多社会福利项目的拆解。快克毒品风暴和去机构化当然也无济于事。无论如何，纽约的无家可归现象尤为爆发，人们有一种感觉，街上的一些人可能会对自己或他人构成危险。如果他们符合这一标准，只要能做到，我们会自愿将他们送往医院，说服他们去；如果必要的话，我们也会非自愿地把他们送去，我们会报警，有时他们会被戴上手铐带到贝尔维尤精神科急诊室。山姆认为有时非自愿收治是

7
