it was necessary, but he was never completely comfortable with it. Sam had ended up in New York City for grad school, where he got interested in the psychiatric survivors movement. The movement challenged the traditional paternalism of psychiatry and promoted the idea that patients should control their own care. This was the future Sam wanted, which put him at odds sometimes with his co-workers. We ended up in Grand Central Station one night. The team was responding to a call about a homeless person that they referred to as the cat
必要的，但他对此从未完全感到自在。山姆最终来到纽约市读研究生，在那里他对精神病幸存者运动产生了兴趣。这场运动挑战了精神病学的传统家长式作风，并提倡患者应该控制自己的护理的理念。这是山姆想要的未来，这有时使他与同事产生矛盾。一天晚上，我们最终来到了中央车站。团队正在处理一个关于一个无家可归者的求助电话，他们把这个人称作猫

8
