woman. Because she loved cats and when she was outside she'd have a cat sometimes with her. She always wore black, completely black outfits. And she was in the bathroom, the women's bathroom of a grand central station where she would stay. And she was like, leave me alone. I hate you people. They thought, oh, she's in denial of her desperate situation, she's not safe. So they bring her to the hospital. I was very upset by that.
女士。因为她喜欢猫，当她在外面时，有时会随身带一只猫。她总是穿黑色，全黑的衣服。她待在中央车站的女洗手间里，那是她落脚的地方。她当时就像是在说，离我远点。我讨厌你们这些人。他们觉得，哦，她对自己的绝望处境处于否认状态，她不安全。于是他们把她带到了医院。对此我感到非常不安。

9
00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:25.000
This was not a situation Sam thought called for involuntary commitment. And so he made an anonymous call to the legal aid program in the hospital. I said, I don't want to say who I am, I just want to tell you about a situation that's in the hospital right now. There's this woman that was hospitalized involuntarily. I think she needs representation. She wants to be out of the hospital. This was an early sign that Sam was generally on team patient over a team psychiatrist. Still, he worked like this for a couple more years, driving around the city,
