We would tell them as little as possible. Sam said they would tell people basically we're working with low-income clients helping them find housing but not we're working with formerly homeless severely mentally ill clients who are also struggling with addiction. They also had people on staff whose specific job it was to communicate with landlords and it helped Sam said that they were always able to guarantee the rent would be paid. Pathways clients would have to put 30% of their incomes toward rent, but the rest would be covered.
我们会尽可能少地透露。山姆说，他们基本上会告诉人们，我们正在与低收入客户合作，帮助他们找到住房，但不会说我们正在与曾经无家可归、患有严重精神疾病且还在与毒瘾作斗争的客户合作。他们的员工中也有专门负责与房东沟通的人，山姆说，这很有帮助，因为他们总是能够保证房租按时支付。“通往住房之路”的客户必须将他们收入的30%用于支付房租，其余部分则由机构覆盖。

